<title>FRANCE: Axa, UAP offer not valid in U.S..</title>
<headline>Axa, UAP offer not valid in U.S..</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurers Axa and UAP said on Tuesday in a statement that their stock swap offer was not valid in the United States.</p>
<p>&quot;The exchange offer is not being made to persons in the United States,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>The companies also said the shares and certificates of guaranteed value being offered to UAP shareholders in the deal would not be registered under the U.S. Securities Act of 1933.</p>
<p>Axa and UAP are to swap four Axa shares and four certificates of guaranteed value for 10 UAP shares under merger terms announced on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
